ir, T5,T8 singles.  \n\n**Evaluation**: Chi T5 uses T3 and T4 (two tiles not helping much otherwise) and retains T5, T7 pair, B5 triple. Leaves more pairs for seven pairs possibility? But 6 tiles left not 7. Actually 6 tiles: T5, T7\u00d72, T8, B5\u00d73 \u2014 B5 triple counts as 3 same, not as 2 separate pairs for seven pairs. So no seven pairs.  \n\nBetter maybe Chi T7: keeps T3, T4\u00d72, T7, T8, B5\u00d73 \u2014 has T4 pair, close to chow T3,T4,T5 later if draw T5, or T4,T5,T6 if draw T5,T6 (T6 dead though), so not great.  \n\nBut looking at all: B5 triple could be concealed pung for points, plus maybe Dragon Pung (no), Seat Wind (no), but All Simples possible if no honors/terminals (yes currently).  \n\nBest to aim for All Simples + Concealed Hand + maybe Triple Pung if get other triples.  \n\n**Given unshown tiles counts**: T5 (4 left), T7 (4 left), T8 (4 left), T4 (2 left) \u2014 T4 rare.  \n\nMaybe keep the T4\u00d72 for pair/chow potential. That suggests **Chi T6** (using T4,T5) reduces T4 count to 1 \u2014 worse.  \nChi T7 (using T5,T7) keeps T4\u00d72 \u2014 better.  \nChi T5 (using T3,T4) reduces T4 to 1 \u2014 worse.  \n\nAlso B5: 3 left in my hand, unshown shows 3 more available \u2014 possible kong later.  \n\nThus **Chi T7** keeps T4 pair and T3 for potential chow if draw T5.  \n\nGiven meld [W5,W6,W7] is a chow, if I get All Chows pattern maybe? That requires 4 chows + pair. Currently: 1 chow (W5-W7), after chi T7 \u2192 2 chows, leaves T3,T4,T4,T8,B5\u00d73 \u2014 still far from all chows.  \n\nActually, with B5 triple, can\u2019t have all chows (pung not chow). So maybe change plan: aim for All Pungs (6 points) + All Simples (2 points) = 8 points enough to win. That means need 4 pungs/kongs. Currently: B5 triple is one potential pung/kong, need 3 more. Hard with current hand.  \n\nSo maybe better to not chi at all \u2014 keep hand closed for chance at Concealed Hand (4 points) + Self-Drawn (1) + All Simples (2) + maybe Pung of simples (1) = 8 if