n an exposed one).  \n\n**Reason:**  \nPassing maintains more hand flexibility and retains possibilities for concealed patterns, while Peng T7 would commit to an exposed meld and force a discard that could break potential combinations. Given the game is not in the late stage (still many tiles unseen), I choose to Pass.  \n\n**Answer:** Pass"}
